<title>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 2</title>
<!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View><w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]-->
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #1a1a2e; line-height: 1.4; }
h1 { font-size: 20pt; color: #0b2e6b; border-bottom: 2px solid #0b2e6b; padding-bottom: 4pt; }
h2 { font-size: 15pt; color: #0b2e6b; margin-top: 16pt; }
h3 { font-size: 12.5pt; color: #14213d; margin-top: 12pt; }
hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #b0b8c4; }
strong { color: #0b2e6b; }
blockquote { background: #eef2f7; border-left: 3pt solid #0b2e6b; margin: 8pt 0; padding: 6pt 12pt; font-style: italic; }
ul, ol { margin: 6pt 0 6pt 12pt; }
li { margin: 3pt 0; }
code { font-family: Consolas, monospace; background: #eef2f7; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 10pt 0; font-size: 10.5pt; }
th { background: #0b2e6b; color: #ffffff; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #9aa5b4; padding: 4pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 2</h1>
<p><strong>Name: ____________________   Date: __________   Score: ______ / 100</strong></p>
<p>Closed book. Answer in the voice of the agent handling the ticket. For each scenario, state <strong>how you handle it</strong> (route + action) and <strong>the one trap</strong> that would fail the ticket. <strong>Section A — 6 points each; Section B (multiple choice) — 2 points each. Total 100.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1.</strong> <em>"Tracking says my package was delivered yesterday, but nothing came. I checked with my neighbors and the porch — it's not here."</em> How do you handle a "marked delivered, not received" ticket?</p>
<p><strong>Q2.</strong> <em>"I placed my team order 3 weeks ago and it still just says 'Awaiting Fulfillment.' Where is it?"</em> What do you check, and what timeline do you quote for a mandatory team kit?</p>
<p><strong>Q3.</strong> <em>"I clearly ordered a size Large jersey — my confirmation says Large — but you shipped me a Medium."</em> Whose fault is this, and what's the correct handling?</p>
<p><strong>Q4.</strong> <em>"I want to return my son's kit — it has his name and number 10 printed on it — because he's changed clubs."</em> What is the policy, and how do you respond?</p>
<p><strong>Q5.</strong> <em>"I got an email weeks ago saying my refund was processed, but I still don't see it on my credit card."</em> How do you handle a refund-status follow-up?</p>
<p><strong>Q6.</strong> <em>"I keep trying to check out on my iPhone but I can't even find the cart button. The site is broken."</em> What's the correct guidance?</p>
<p><strong>Q7.</strong> <em>"Another mom sent me her son's ordering link, but I need my own link for my son to order his kit."</em> How do you handle this?</p>
<p><strong>Q8.</strong> <em>"The size I need is out of stock and you have no restock date. I need something for the season — what can you do?"</em> What can you offer?</p>
<p><strong>Q9.</strong> <em>"We placed our mandatory kit order but got charged for the 'complimentary' hoodie that was supposed to be free."</em> How do you handle this?</p>
<p><strong>Q10. Multi-issue ticket.</strong> <em>"I paid three weeks ago and never got a confirmation email, I can't get into the Lightning FC store, and while you're at it I'd like to add a keeper jersey to my order."</em> Break this into its separate issues, route each one, and state the correct answer for each.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Section B — Multiple Choice (Q11–Q30)</h2>
<p>Choose the single best answer. 2 points each.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> Refund timing to quote for a <strong>Shopify</strong> cancellation:</p>
<ul><li>A) 3–5 business days</li><li>B) Up to two weeks</li><li>C) 24 hours</li><li>D) 30 days</li></ul>
<p><strong>12.</strong> Return shipping costs are:</p>
<ul><li>A) Fully refunded</li><li>B) Refunded as store credit</li><li>C) Not refunded</li><li>D) Half refunded</li></ul>
<p><strong>13.</strong> A mandatory-kit item returned on its own is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refundable anytime</li><li>B) Not returnable alone; refunded once a correct-size new order is placed &amp; received</li><li>C) Freely exchangeable</li><li>D) Never refundable</li></ul>
<p><strong>14.</strong> FBB stands for:</p>
<ul><li>A) Fulfilled By Buyer</li><li>B) Fast Bulk Batch</li><li>C) Fulfilled By Bangladesh</li><li>D) Fulfilled By Brand</li></ul>
<p><strong>15.</strong> All Shopify / capellisport.com orders are:</p>
<ul><li>A) FBPA</li><li>B) FBB</li><li>C) Referee orders</li><li>D) International only</li></ul>
<p><strong>16.</strong> An evidence photo request should ask the customer to show:</p>
<ul><li>A) Their face</li><li>B) The size tag</li><li>C) The receipt</li><li>D) Only the packaging</li></ul>
<p><strong>17.</strong> A windbreaker's reflective dots are damaged after one wear. This is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Not covered (non-decoration)</li><li>B) The customer's fault</li><li>C) Covered — request a photo, then a same-size replacement</li><li>D) A standard return</li></ul>
<p><strong>18.</strong> CS.com (capellisport.com) processing time:</p>
<ul><li>A) 5 weeks</li><li>B) 3–4 business days</li><li>C) 2 weeks</li><li>D) 5–10 business days</li></ul>
<p><strong>19.</strong> Referee-club processing time:</p>
<ul><li>A) 5 weeks</li><li>B) 24 hours</li><li>C) 3–4 business days</li><li>D) 5–10 business days</li></ul>
<p><strong>20.</strong> After a guest order, to view status / order individual items the customer must:</p>
<ul><li>A) Do nothing</li><li>B) Call CS</li><li>C) Create an account with the same email and have the order linked</li><li>D) Reorder</li></ul>
<p><strong>21.</strong> When a customer's order is returned to sender, you first:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refund immediately</li><li>B) Reship to the same address</li><li>C) Cancel the order</li><li>D) Confirm the correct address, then reship</li></ul>
<p><strong>22.</strong> A complimentary item was charged (a club-wide issue). You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refund on the spot</li><li>B) Escalate to the internal team; set Open + internal note</li><li>C) Ignore it</li><li>D) Ask for a photo</li></ul>
<p><strong>23.</strong> Two players on one account: after adding player 1's kit you:</p>
<ul><li>A) Check out immediately</li><li>B) Select "Proceed to Cart", then add player 2's kit and check out</li><li>C) Create a second account</li><li>D) Call CS</li></ul>
<p><strong>24.</strong> Which timeline is for <strong>in-stock</strong> items?</p>
<ul><li>A) 3–7 business days</li><li>B) 3–6 weeks</li><li>C) 5 weeks</li><li>D) 24 hours</li></ul>
<p><strong>25.</strong> Pre-order items take about:</p>
<ul><li>A) 3–7 business days</li><li>B) 2 weeks</li><li>C) 3–6 weeks</li><li>D) 5 weeks</li></ul>
<p><strong>26.</strong> A repeat defect (same problem on the replacement) should be:</p>
<ul><li>A) Reshipped identically</li><li>B) Refunded silently</li><li>C) Escalated; confirm corrected artwork before reshipping</li><li>D) Ignored</li></ul>
<p><strong>27.</strong> Wrong-club decoration on a whole team requires:</p>
<ul><li>A) A blind reship</li><li>B) A photo of all affected items + escalation</li><li>C) A refund only</li><li>D) No action</li></ul>
<p><strong>28.</strong> Phone support at Capelli is:</p>
<ul><li>A) 24/7</li><li>B) Business hours only</li><li>C) Not offered — email only</li><li>D) For VIPs only</li></ul>
<p><strong>29.</strong> A customer asks for their replacement's RO number to track it. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Give the RO number</li><li>B) Explain you'll send the tracking number once it ships</li><li>C) Give them the internal note</li><li>D) Refuse with no alternative</li></ul>
<p><strong>30.</strong> When you're waiting on customer photos, the ticket status should be:</p>
<ul><li>A) Solved</li><li>B) Pending</li><li>C) Closed</li><li>D) Merged</li></ul></body></html>